  displayName: Wampanoag
  leader: Ousamequin (Massasoit)
  date: c. 1623
  biography: Ousamequin was a Pokanoket sachem within the Wampanoag world. A 1623 account describes a broad wampum belt and a black wolfskin over his shoulder.
  region: Southern New England; present-day Massachusetts and Rhode Island.
  terrain:
  - Broadleaf Forest
  - Prairie
  - Swamp
  goods:
  - Food
  - Fur
  jobs:
  - Farmers
  - Fur Trappers
  rival: Narragansett
  scenarioAggression: Low
  contextNote: Use Narragansett as a scenario rival inspired by early seventeenth-century regional tensions; alliances also changed over time.
